[
  {
    "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The scene features a rustic, seasoned cast-iron skillet centered in the frame, containing a hearty serving of white bean and zucchini pizza bake for two people. The composition is captured at a 3/4 overhead angle, ensuring the texture of the bubbling, golden-brown melted mozzarella and parmesan layer is fully visible across the entire surface. Beneath the molten cheese, chunks of caramelized cremini mushrooms, sautéed tender zucchini, and creamy navy beans are visible, coated in a rich, rustic crushed tomato sauce. The dish is placed on a worn, weathered oak wood table. Shallow depth of field keeps the skillet sharp while the background softly blurs. Soft, natural side light from a window on the left creates subtle highlights on the bubbling cheese and oil droplets. Props include a casual, worn wooden spoon resting beside the skillet and a slightly rumpled linen napkin tucked near the base. A few scattered dried oregano flakes and a small stray piece of sautéed zucchini lie naturally on the wood surface near the skillet. The scene reflects a lived-in, warm home kitchen. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The dish shows authentic signs of home cooking: slight sauce drips on the skillet rim, uneven browning of the cheese, and a rustic, non-symmetrical arrangement. Warm, golden-hour color temperature, cozy and inviting. No plastic sheen, no perfect symmetry. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. The image is indistinguishable from a professional cookbook photograph."
  }
]
